# GitHub Project board hygiene

When doing substantive work on a named effort (analysis, model, pipeline, SOP, deliverable):

## If a project board exists

1. Identify the matching GitHub Project (e.g. via `gh project list` / linked repo projects).
2. Map the current task to the relevant board item (draft issue or issue).
3. **Update the item as you work**, not only at the end:
   - Status: Todo → In Progress when starting; Done when finished
   - Title/body: reflect scope changes, decisions, blockers
   - Start date / Target date / Sprint / Priority when the plan shifts
   - Add a short note in the body when a deliverable lands (path, PR, or result summary)
4. Prefer `gh project item-edit` (and related `gh project` commands) over leaving board state stale.

## If no project board exists

- **Ask the user** whether to create one before continuing large multi-step work.
- If they agree, create a GitHub Project linked to the repo, seed cards from the stated scope/proposal, and set a time window when they give one.
- Do not invent a board silently.

## Scope

Applies to ongoing delivery work. Skip for tiny one-off Q&A with no project context.
